<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Strength Through Joy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1933">1933</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kraft durch Freude</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Strength Through Joy was the leisure organisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-labour-front">German Labour Front</a>, founded in November 1933. It offered workers cheap holidays, cruises, concerts, sport and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, aiming to win support for the regime and raise productivity, and it began the giant seaside resort of Prora on Rügen. The Volkswagen car was first promoted as the KdF-Wagen, after the organisation's German initials.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/strength-through-joy.jpg" alt="Strength Through Joy" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ericmetro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KdF_Symbol.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
